# SeatRelay — variables the scripts read from the shell. Copy to `.env`, fill in, then load it:
#   bash / Git Bash / WSL / macOS:  set -a; source .env; set +a
#   PowerShell:                     Get-Content .env | ? {$_ -match '^\w+='} | % { $n,$v = $_ -split '=',2; Set-Item env:$n $v }
# Nothing auto-loads this file (no dotenv); `.env` and `.env.*` are git-ignored, only this example is
# tracked. Never paste a key into chat, a screenshot or a commit (docs/aws-setup.md §H: deactivate it).
#
# What you need depends on what you run:
#   - local stack (docker compose, no AWS):      nothing below; see services/local/README.md
#   - web app on your laptop against the dev stage: nothing below; see README §4 "Laptop"
#   - deploy, experiments, e2e walkthrough, seeding on dev/pilot: the AWS block + the test password

# --- AWS (IAM user seatrelay-deployer; each member creates their own access key, docs/aws-setup.md §C) ---
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIA................
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=........................................
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=ap-southeast-1

# --- Test accounts on the AWS stages (walkthrough-*, demo.*, loaduser-*, study accounts) ---
# One shared private password, chosen by whoever (re)creates the accounts; hand it over in person or
# through a password manager. The scripts refuse the public local-stack default on an AWS stage.
# To set a new one: SEATRELAY_TEST_PASSWORD=<new> tools/e2e/bin/ensure-users.sh (walkthrough accounts),
# pnpm --filter @seatrelay/scripts create-test-users -- --count 60 (experiment pool),
# pnpm --filter @seatrelay/scripts seed-demo -- --target dev (demo accounts).
SEATRELAY_TEST_PASSWORD=
# E2E_PASSWORD=            # tools/e2e only; falls back to SEATRELAY_TEST_PASSWORD

# --- Deploy scripts (tools/scripts/bin/deploy-all.sh, deploy-web.sh, teardown.sh) ---
STAGE=dev                  # dev | pilot
# ALARM_EMAIL=             # CloudWatch alarm subscription of the app stack (team mailbox)
# SENDER_EMAIL=            # SES sender identity (auth stack); leave unset to keep the current one
# BUDGET_EMAIL=            # AWS Budgets notifications (auth stack)
# EMAIL_ENABLED=true       # notifier sends e-mail (true on both stages since 24 Oct 2026)
# AUTH_STACK=seatrelay-auth

# --- Optional shortcuts for tools/scripts and tools/experiments (otherwise read from CloudFormation) ---
# TARGET_API=https://3s8s2lavzi.execute-api.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com   # dev ApiUrl
# COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=ap-southeast-1_ZZ7UsL6Ib
# COGNITO_TOOLING_CLIENT_ID=203uigcnditpcmp54ir0gnsieq

# --- tools/e2e walkthrough ---
# E2E_STAGE=dev            # or --stage dev
# E2E_WEB_URL=             # override the stage's CloudFront URL (e.g. a vite preview on http://localhost:5173)
# E2E_PREFIX=              # account prefix (default walkthrough)
# E2E_SCALE=               # viewport scale
# CHROMIUM_PATH=           # Chrome binary when Playwright's own download is not used
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=

# --- Local on-prem reference (docker compose) and load tests ---
# PG_CONTAINER=seatrelay-local-postgres-1   # empty = experiments skip the Postgres side channel
# K6_BIN=k6
# RUNS=3                   # tools/experiments/bin/run-table3.sh
# VITE_OIDC_PROVIDER / VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY / VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID / VITE_HOSTED_UI_DOMAIN / VITE_API_BASE_URL
#   are read only by the nginx container of the local stack (services/local/nginx/entrypoint.sh); the
#   Vite dev server reads apps/web/public/env.js instead.
